      "artist": "Shrabanti Mitra",
      "description": "Kurumbera fort is located in the village of Gaganeshwar, which is 4 km from Keshiari and 30 km from Kharagpur. According to an Odia inscription at the fort, it was built between 1438 and 1469, during the rule of the Surya Vamsi king of Odisha, Gajapati Kapilendra Dev. However, Kurumbera also has structures built during the Mughal emperor Aurangazeb’s reign (1658-1707) by one Mohammed Tahir, according to another stone inscription.",
